# Next.js App Router File Conventions

Apply these conventions for this repository:

- `@docs/CONVENTIONS.md` is the single source of truth for project conventions.
- Whenever adding/changing a convention, update `@docs/CONVENTIONS.md` in the same task.
- Keep route files in `web/src/app` only (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `route.ts`).
- Use route group `web/src/app/(client)` for public pages.
- Keep admin pages under `web/src/app/(admin)/admin/*` for a cleaner tree.
- Keep authenticated user pages under `web/src/app/(user)/user/*` (separate from admin).
- Keep domain logic in `web/src/features/<feature-name>`.
- Keep shared UI in `web/src/components/ui`; keep shared layout/widgets in `web/src/components/common`.
- Keep technical helpers in `web/src/lib` (`env.ts`, `db.ts`, `auth.ts`, `utils.ts`).
- Keep shared types in `web/src/types`.
- Media library UI should live at `web/src/app/(admin)/admin/(protected)/media/page.tsx`.
- Media API should live at `web/src/app/api/media/route.ts`.
- Local uploads should be stored in `web/public/uploads/*` with metadata in `web/storage/media.json`.
- User Login page should live at `web/src/app/(user)/user/(auth)/login/page.tsx`.
- User Register page should live at `web/src/app/(user)/user/(auth)/register/page.tsx`.
- Admin Login page should live at `web/src/app/(admin)/admin/(auth)/login/page.tsx`.
- Auth APIs should live under `web/src/app/api/auth/*`.
- Admin account/role APIs should live under `web/src/app/api/admin/users/*`.

## Naming

- Folders and utility files: `kebab-case`.
- React component files: `PascalCase.tsx`.
- Variables/functions: `camelCase`.
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.

## App Router boundaries

- Prefer Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed.
- Keep API handlers under `web/src/app/api/**/route.ts`.
- Route-specific components stay in that route folder, e.g. `_components`.
- Prefer route groups for layout separation where needed (currently `(client)`).

## Feature module pattern

Inside `web/src/features/<feature-name>/`, prefer:

- `components/`
- `actions.ts`
- `service.ts`
- `schema.ts`
- `types.ts`

## Imports

- Prefer `@/` absolute imports over deep relative paths.
- Avoid importing server-only code into client components.
